## FAQ

Q: Does it work with any web server?
A: Yes. ModPageSpeed 2.0 deploys as a reverse proxy in front of any HTTP origin — Apache, Node.js, Python, Ruby, PHP, or any other backend.

Q: Do I need to change my application code?
A: No. All optimization is transparent at the reverse-proxy level.

Q: What about HTTP/2?
A: Yes. The nginx interceptor supports HTTP/2 and HTTP/3.

Q: Can I disable specific optimizations?
A: Yes. Use --disable-image, --disable-css, --disable-js, or --disable-html worker flags.

Q: What happens on the first request?
A: The first request serves the original content (X-PageSpeed: MISS). The worker optimizes asynchronously. Subsequent requests get optimized content (X-PageSpeed: HIT).

Q: Is there a Kubernetes deployment option?
A: Yes. Run nginx and worker as sidecar containers in the same pod sharing an emptyDir volume.

