SvelteKit application served at /console/ by the worker (port 9880). Eight pages: Dashboard (live metrics, charts, alerts), URL Inspector (cache contents, variant detail, device simulation), Waterfall Viewer (network timing via headless Chrome), Visual Diff (before/after screenshot comparison), Configuration (hot-reload settings, export/import, snapshots), Metrics (flat counter/gauge table), Bandwidth Savings (impact measurement), Debug Console (real-time log streaming). Connects via REST + WebSocket. Optional API token authentication.

## Browser Analysis

Optional headless Chrome pipeline for browser-validated optimization. Uses CDP over pipe transport (FD 3/4). Components: BrowserCssExtractor (CSS Coverage API), PageAnalyzer (LCP, fold, CLS, image dims), UnusedCssRemover, VisualRegressionGate (pixel diff), FontGlyphScanner, ScriptCoverageAnalyzer (Profiler coverage + deferral categories). Four-layer SSRF defense. Chrome process recycled every 100 pages, RSS-monitored. Template-based profiling via FNV-1a DOM hashing. Optimization policy engine computes per-template decisions (async CSS, script deferral) from browser analysis data. Enable with --enable-browser-analysis.

